menu "Board: RGB LCD timing"

    config BOARD_LCD_PCLK_MHZ
        int "Pixel clock (MHz)"
        range 8 21
        default 16
        help
            RGB panel pixel clock. 16 MHz is the Waveshare reference value
            (about 39 frames/s). If text shows a faint shadow smeared to the
            side, try a lower clock (12-14). Higher than 18 needs the bounce
            buffer and may drift while Wi-Fi/flash are busy.

    config BOARD_LCD_PCLK_ACTIVE_NEG
        bool "Sample data on the falling PCLK edge"
        default y
        help
            The panel latches RGB data on this PCLK edge. The Waveshare
            reference uses the falling edge (y). If every edge in the image
            has a shadow or a 1-pixel ghost, try the other edge (n).

    config BOARD_LCD_HSYNC_BACK_PORCH
        int "HSYNC back porch (PCLK cycles)"
        range 4 80
        default 8
        help
            Reference value 8. A larger value (e.g. 40) moves the start of each
            line later; it does not change the picture if the panel uses DE.

endmenu
